---
/**
 * Our Team (/team) — Consultancy. Built against the committed Figma node 8187:8979
 * (design/figma/fTqnnV20l9htP7vFJrOsvn/8187-8979/), see docs/consultancy-build-plan.md.
 *
 * Not linked from the shared header/footer nav (`src/lib/nav.ts`) — confirmed against Home's
 * own node.json in Phase 1 (not an oversight), so this route is intentionally unlinked but
 * still built, tested, and held to the same a11y/visual gates as every other route.
 *
 * Typography confirmed against node.json (not guessed):
 *   - Hero "Our Team": 64/56/700/-0.26 (`--font-size-hero` + `--line-height-h2`/
 *     `--letter-spacing-h2`) — the same one-off composition Services'/About's hero titles use,
 *     not the hero role's own 72px/-3.3. Same photo (imageRef `55fffb0d…`, the shared
 *     lecture-hall stock shot Home/About/Services already reuse) with a baked-in 25% black
 *     scrim, bottom-anchored/centred — reused verbatim from `.about-hero`.
 *   - No section heading precedes the team grid — confirmed by the node tree (the grid's
 *     parent, 8187:9246, has exactly two children: the grid and the CTA card; no heading/
 *     eyebrow node exists, hidden or otherwise). Unlike Home's "Core Team" section (which has
 *     an eyebrow+h2+paragraph intro before its 4-card row), Team jumps straight from the hero
 *     H1 into the grid. Confirmed per this page's own node.json, not assumed from Home's
 *     precedent — the build plan's instruction to check every recurring pattern per-page
 *     (About's `u-h2` vs `u-section-title` finding) applies here too.
 *   - Member card: the same Figma component Home's Core Team instantiates (node 8090:7151),
 *     so it lives in `TeamCard.astro` — including its progressive backdrop blur and the
 *     Inter→Arial typography call. See that file for the confirmed geometry and rationale.
 *   - The closing CTA band is the shared `CtaSection.astro`. This page's node.json agrees with
 *     Home's, Services' and About's byte-for-byte, so it is instantiated rather than
 *     re-authored; see that file for the confirmed content and geometry.
 *
 * Content notes confirmed via node.json (not guessed):
 *   - The design's 10 member cards (4 + 4 + 2, matching the source's exact row split) all carry
 *     the identical placeholder name/role/photo — the same not-yet-personalised pattern as
 *     Home's Core Team (4×) and Services'/Home's other repeated content. Those ten were
 *     hard-coded here until 2026-08-14; the roster now comes from the CMS (see below) and the
 *     placeholders survive only as `@lib/staff`'s fixtures, so a build with no API still renders
 *     this frame exactly as designed.
 *   - Grid gaps confirmed from node.json's auto-layout: 24px between cards in a row
 *     (`--space-md`), 80px between rows (`--space-4xl`) — a genuine distinction from Home's
 *     single-row Core Team section, which only ever needed one gap value.
 *
 * ## The roster is CMS-driven
 *
 * Members come from `@lib/staff` at build time (`GET /api/staff/all`, admin-authored via the
 * dashboard's AdminStaff screen). The grid is the design's, unchanged — only its contents moved.
 * Two consequences worth knowing:
 *
 *   - **The row split is no longer 4+4+2.** It's whatever `ceil(n / 4)` gives, because the real
 *     roster decides `n`. The 4-column grid, both gaps and the responsive collapse are untouched,
 *     so any count lands on the design's own geometry.
 *   - **Publishing a member needs a rebuild.** Static output; see `@lib/cms`.
 *
 * Home's Core Team section draws from the same module, sliced to the design's first four. This
 * page is the full roster; Home's is the taster.
 *
 * Component reuse considered: `ServiceDetailSection` (the ★ template) shapes a
 * title+subtitle/about-covers-cost block — Team's content (a photo grid + the shared CTA) isn't
 * that shape, so this page writes its own markup, same call as About's.
 */
import BaseLayout from '@layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import TeamCard from '@components/TeamCard.astro';
import CtaSection from '@components/CtaSection.astro';
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import { teamHeroPhoto, teamMemberPhoto } from '@lib/team-images';
import { getStaff } from '@lib/staff';

const team = await getStaff();
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Our Team — GIEVA Consultancy"
  description="Meet the GIEVA Consultancy team guiding every student through their global education journey."
  brand="consultancy"
>
  <!-- ── Hero ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
  <section class="team-hero">
    <div class="team-hero__media">
      <Image src={teamHeroPhoto} alt="" width={1440} height={670} class="team-hero__photo" />
      <div class="team-hero__scrim" aria-hidden="true"></div>
    </div>
    <div class="container team-hero__content">
      <h1 class="team-hero__heading">Our Team</h1>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ── Team grid ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
  <section class="section team-grid-section">
    <div class="container">
      {
        team.length > 0 ? (
          <ul role="list" class="team-grid">
            {team.map((member) => (
              <li>
                {/* No photo uploaded → the design's own placeholder portrait, which is a local
                    asset and so goes through astro:assets. A card with an empty frame would read
                    as a broken image; the placeholder reads as "photo pending". */}
                <TeamCard
                  src={member.imageUrl ?? teamMemberPhoto}
                  name={member.name}
                  role={member.role}
                />
              </li>
            ))}
          </ul>
        ) : (
          /* A real state, not a placeholder — same call as /ngo/resources. The CMS starts empty,
             and this page is reachable by URL before the first member is published. Says so
             plainly instead of rendering an empty grid under a lone "Our Team" hero. */
          <p class="u-body-lg team-empty">
            Team profiles are on their way. In the meantime,{' '}
            <a class="u-underline" href="/about">
              read about GIEVA
            </a>{' '}
            or{' '}
            <a class="u-underline" href="/services">
              see what we do
            </a>
            .
          </p>
        )
      }
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ── CTA (same content/shape as Home's/Services'/About's) ───────────────────── -->
  <section class="section cta">
    <div class="container">
      <CtaSection />
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  /* ── Shared section rhythm (matches Home/Services/About) ─────────────────── */
  .section {
    padding-block: var(--section-padding-block);
  }

  /* ── Hero ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
  .team-hero {
    position: relative;
  }
  .team-hero__media {
    position: relative;
  }
  .team-hero__photo {
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    display: block;
  }
  .team-hero__scrim {
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
    background: rgb(0 0 0 / 0.25);
  }
  .team-hero__content {
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-end;
    justify-content: center;
    padding-bottom: var(--space-6xl);
  }
  .team-hero__heading {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--color-white);
    font-family: var(--font-family-base);
    font-size: var(--font-size-hero);
    line-height: var(--line-height-h2);
    letter-spacing: var(--letter-spacing-h2);
    font-weight: var(--font-weight-bold);
    text-align: center;
    overflow-wrap: anywhere;
  }

  /* ── Team grid ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
  .team-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(4, minmax(0, 1fr));
    column-gap: var(--space-md);
    row-gap: var(--space-4xl);
  }
  /* Card itself lives in `TeamCard.astro` — the canonical implementation shared with Home. */

  /* Empty roster. Same measure as /ngo/resources' empty state so the two read as one system. */
  .team-empty {
    max-width: 60ch;
    color: var(--color-text-default);
  }

  /* ── CTA (same content/shape as Home's/Services'/About's) ──────────────── */
  /* The CTA band's styles live in src/components/CtaSection.astro, which owns the
     markup for all four Consultancy pages. */

  /* ── Responsive ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
  @media (max-width: 1024px) {
    .team-grid {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    }
  }
  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .team-hero__heading {
      font-size: var(--font-size-h3);
    }
    .team-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }
</style>
